{
  "statement": "A row typed straight into a thread is made right where it is: a real title, several typed things become several rows in the same thread, a title that is already good is left alone, a sentence stays as typed because there is no note here, and the thread's rules apply. Nothing leaves the thread and nothing is said.",
  "why": "The floor is what they typed, in the thread they chose, saved before the model runs. Everything the turn does is an improvement on something already safe, so doing nothing is a correct outcome and a rewrite that adds nothing is worse than none.",
  "sources": [
    "quick_add.md",
    "005 the thread page (quick add)",
    "harness/plan.py: plan_quick_add"
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "already-good-left-alone",
      "why": "a good title needs nothing",
      "surface": "quick_add",
      "input": "Fix the tap",
      "context": "behrooz",
      "thread_id": "00000013-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "expect": {
        "untouched": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lowercase-left-alone",
      "why": "case alone is not worth a rewrite (labelled 2026-09-17)",
      "surface": "quick_add",
      "input": "fix the tap",
      "context": "behrooz",
      "thread_id": "00000013-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "expect": {
        "untouched": true
      }
    },
    {
